from cp14.replay
# The team from here on (docs/decisions.md "CP15–19 start from a set team"):
# Empoleon, the starter, at a late-game level with TM moves (Ice Beam), three a player plausibly
# has caught and raised (Gible in Wayward Cave, Shinx on Route 202, Starly on Route 201) with level-up and TM moves
# (Earthquake; the elemental fangs), and Bibarel (the HM user) last, so the battle auto policy's next Pokémon after a
# faint is a fighter.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_EMPOLEON 68 platinum:MOVE_SURF platinum:MOVE_ICE_BEAM platinum:MOVE_FLASH_CANNON platinum:MOVE_DRILL_PECK
party 1 platinum:SPECIES_GARCHOMP 67 platinum:MOVE_EARTHQUAKE platinum:MOVE_DRAGON_CLAW platinum:MOVE_CRUNCH platinum:MOVE_FIRE_FANG
party 2 platinum:SPECIES_LUXRAY 65 platinum:MOVE_THUNDER_FANG platinum:MOVE_CRUNCH platinum:MOVE_ICE_FANG platinum:MOVE_FIRE_FANG
party 3 platinum:SPECIES_STARAPTOR 65 platinum:MOVE_BRAVE_BIRD platinum:MOVE_CLOSE_COMBAT platinum:MOVE_AERIAL_ACE platinum:MOVE_QUICK_ATTACK
party 4 platinum:SPECIES_BIBAREL 20 platinum:MOVE_STRENGTH platinum:MOVE_ROCK_CLIMB platinum:MOVE_WATER_GUN platinum:MOVE_HEADBUTT
# CP15 (docs/research/story-cp5-19.md §15): from CP14's end in the Galactic HQ control
# room, out through Veilstone, west over Route 215 and Route 210 to Solaceon, Route 209, Hearthome and Route 208 to
# Mt. Coronet; up the mountain to Spear Pillar (grunts 521 and 527 together, Mars 528 and Jupiter 407 with Barry),
# the Distortion World (the boulders, Cyrus 404), Giratina, Sendoff Spring, and Rowan's lab in Sandgem: lab state 3.
